  "TourPoints": [
    {
      "Id": "db6ad0fe-6590-439f-b010-b87dee124e27",
      "Description": "This chapter focuses on generating geometry.\nAs mentioned earlier, each mesh consists of two buffers stored on the GPU.\nOne buffer contains a list of vertices (corner points), and the second contains a list of triangles defined by references to three of these vertices."
    },
    {
      "Id": "c3dddcd8-bc69-42aa-943f-1b94009dec32",
      "Description": "You may remember the [Transform] operator and how it can be stacked to build increasingly complex transformations.\nThe [TransformMesh] operator looks similar, has the same parameters, and produces the same visual result.\nHowever, it works very differently.\nEach [TransformMesh] creates a **new mesh**."
    },
    {
      "Id": "4867fbf3-6503-44f0-b6c9-e6b6aea96f11",
      "Description": "Try to guess how many mesh buffers are used in this example.\nKeep a number in mind before continuing."
    },
    {
      "Id": "f84393d1-a7ab-4bf9-91b5-ab4d3ada7f4a",
      "Description": "It is three.\nThe first buffer contains the original cube.\nThe second buffer contains a rotated copy.\nThe third buffer is a new, larger mesh that combines both.\nThis final buffer is what gets drawn."
    },
    {
      "Id": "ff6b1525-e332-4bfa-898e-7bbca13424d6",
      "Description": "Recreate the example.",
      "Style": "CallToAction"
    }
  ]
}